WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.340
Welcome! Today we are exploring how a hydroelectric

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.370
power station turns the natural movement of water into the

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.520
electricity that powers our homes. Water stored at a

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.450
height behind a dam possesses gravitational potential

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.480
energy. As gravity pulls the water downward, this stored

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.140
energy transforms into the kinetic energy of moving

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.160
water. Next, the rushing water spins a large

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.900
turbine. The spinning turbine drives a generator

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.620
inside the station. Inside the generator, changing

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.210
magnetic fields induce an electric current. Finally, a

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.270
transformer adjusts the voltage so electricity can travel

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.280
safely across power lines. Remember, energy is

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.330
simply converted from one form to another, never created from

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:51.680
nothing.
